# DevLead server — runtime settings for compose.yaml.
#
#   cp docker/devlead.env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# .env (at the repository root) holds secrets: keep it mode 600 and out of git
# (.gitignore already ignores it). compose passes it to the container at start
# and reads DEVLEAD_UID/DEVLEAD_GID from it; nothing in it is copied into the
# image. Values are plain text after the "=", without quotes.

# --- Build (required) ----------------------------------------------------------
# The container runs as your user. Set these to the output of `id -u` and
# `id -g`; compose refuses to build or start while they are empty.
# Changing them needs a rebuild: docker compose up -d --build
# Build with the commit you build from, so doctor.sh can vouch for the image
# (the scheduled claude runs do not start otherwise):
#   DEVLEAD_SOURCE_REV="$(git rev-parse HEAD)" docker compose up -d --build
DEVLEAD_UID=
DEVLEAD_GID=

# --- State shared with your /devlead (S14) ---------------------------------------
# The container reads and writes the state your interactive /devlead reads —
# agenda, decisions, journals, outcomes, reports, run state, the audit log and
# the inbox — so in the morning /devlead sees what was done at night. Only
# those subdirectories of your ~/.devlead are mounted (learn/ read-only),
# never gh-token, notify.env or loop.env. They are written as your user, each
# TSV under flock. Create them once before the first start:
#   mkdir -p ~/.devlead/{agenda,audit,decisions,journals,learn,outcomes,reports,run-state}
#   touch ~/.devlead/inbox.tsv ~/.devlead/inbox.read.tsv
# The absolute path of your ~/.devlead (compose does not expand ~). Required.
DEVLEAD_STATE_DIR=
# Turn off the systemd timers of .devlead/systemd/ when the server runs:
# both would write the same day's report.

# --- Repos the server works on (S13) --------------------------------------------
# The jobs never touch your working copies. The container keeps its own clone
# of each enrolled repo in a Docker volume and resets it to origin's default
# branch before every job: what a run leaves behind in a clone does not reach
# the next one. Each clone sits at the path the repo has on this machine, so
# the morning /devlead finds what the night's runs recorded about it.
# The directory that holds every repo you enroll, as an absolute path (not
# /, /home, or a system directory). The clones volume is mounted at this same
# path inside the container. Required: compose refuses to start without it.
DEVLEAD_WORKSPACE=
# The enrolled repos, comma-separated: <path on this machine>=<owner>/<repo>.
# Each path inside DEVLEAD_WORKSPACE, none inside another; letters, digits and
# . _ @ + - only. This is the server's fleet list (~/.devlead/autonomous-repos
# in the container, root's: no session can add a repo). Give the GitHub token
# below access to exactly these repos. An invalid entry stops the start and is
# named by its position. Each repo's .devlead/envelope.yml, CLAUDE.md and
# .claude/ come from origin's default branch, like its code: commit the
# envelope there, or the server sees that repo as not enrolled.
#   DEVLEAD_REPOS=/home/you/Work/app=you/app,/home/you/Work/api=you/api
DEVLEAD_REPOS=
# The repo the loop job works in: one of the paths above, or empty.
DEVLEAD_LOOP_REPO=
# The loop's plan: the absolute path of your plan file on this machine (e.g.
# /home/you/.devlead/plan.local.yml), or empty. compose mounts it read-only;
# at start root checks it (a tasks list, each task with an id) and installs a
# copy no session can change. An invalid plan stops the start. Restart the
# container after you edit it. With DEVLEAD_LOOP_REPO set and no plan the
# loop job is skipped every night, and the start log says so.
DEVLEAD_LOOP_PLAN=
# The author of the commits the server makes, rendered by root into the
# image's git config: no session can change it. Both are required once a repo
# is enrolled. A GitHub noreply address works:
#   DEVLEAD_GIT_EMAIL=12345+you@users.noreply.github.com
DEVLEAD_GIT_NAME=
DEVLEAD_GIT_EMAIL=

# --- Claude (S12) --------------------------------------------------------------
# Long-lived token for your Claude subscription. On a machine with a browser,
# run `claude setup-token`, approve access, and paste the token it prints.
# One subscription: fill in these two and leave the account pool below empty.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# The day you ran `claude setup-token`, as YYYY-MM-DD. The token lasts one
# year; `devlead doctor` warns from month 11.
DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_TOKEN_ISSUED=

# --- Claude account pool (S21) -------------------------------------------------
# Several subscriptions instead of the single token above (leave those two
# empty: the setups do not mix). Each account has a number, which is its
# priority (1 first, no gaps, at most 9), a short name (a lowercase letter,
# then lowercase letters, digits or -; it names the account in the audit and
# the notices), its own token from `claude setup-token` run while logged in
# to that account, and the day that token was issued (YYYY-MM-DD; doctor warns
# per account from month 11). An invalid account stops the start, named; a
# token is never printed.
#
# Every session uses the highest-priority account that is available, and gets
# that account's token only, with no other variable of the pool. At start the
# tokens move to /etc/devlead/claude-tokens (root's, readable by your group
# only) and out of the environment: only the claude wrapper reads them. When a session ends on that account's usage limit
# (5-hour or weekly), the account rests until the reset time Claude reports
# (5 hours when it reports none) and the next sessions use the next account;
# at the reset, sessions go back to it. The iteration that ended on the limit
# does not count: it runs again at once on the next account, the one-pass
# fleet, poll and discover runs included. An account that never reaches a limit
# is simply never marked. A token Claude refuses (invalid, expired, revoked)
# rests its account until you renew it and restart the container. When every
# account rests, no session starts until the earliest reset, the runs stop
# trying, and one `need` notice says until when (claude-limited). The single
# token above is a pool of one account named "default" and rests the same way.
#
# Example: the team subscription first, so it is used until its 5-hour limit,
# and a personal one as the fallback for that window.
#   DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_1=team
#   DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_1_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...
#   DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_1_ISSUED=2026-11-17
#   DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_2=ultra
#   DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_2_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-...
#   DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_2_ISSUED=2026-11-17
DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_1=
DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_1_TOKEN=
DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_1_ISSUED=
DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_2=
DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_2_TOKEN=
DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_2_ISSUED=

# --- GitHub (S10) --------------------------------------------------------------
# Fine-grained personal access token (GitHub → Settings → Developer settings →
# Fine-grained tokens):
#   Repository access: Only select repositories — the enrolled repos, no others
#   Repository permissions:
#     Contents        Read and write
#     Pull requests   Read and write
#     Issues          Read and write
#     Metadata        Read-only (GitHub adds it on its own)
#   Do NOT grant Workflows, Administration or any other permission. Without
#   Workflows, GitHub rejects any push that changes .github/workflows.
# Backup that only you can turn on: branch protection (or a ruleset) on the
# default branch of every enrolled repo. It is a GitHub setting of each repo
# that you enable yourself; DevLead does not set it.
GH_TOKEN=

# --- Notifications (ntfy) ------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. The URL carries the topic, which is the secret that protects the
# channel. Its host is added to the egress allowlist at start.
DEVLEAD_NTFY_URL=
# Optional, sent as a Bearer token.
DEVLEAD_NTFY_TOKEN=
# 1 adds the repository and the message to the push body (privacy: see
# .devlead/scripts/notify.sh): the PR links of a `pr-opened` notice, the issue
# numbers of a `park` one, the lists of the agenda and of the end of the day.
# Without it the push carries only the notice's code; the local inbox always
# has the message.
DEVLEAD_NOTIFY_DETAIL=

# --- Headless claude runs (S7) ---------------------------------------------------
# The permission flags of every unattended `claude -p` run. Without them the
# runs refuse to start.
DEVLEAD_LOOP_CLAUDE_ARGS=--permission-mode acceptEdits --allowedTools Bash,Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Agent
# Flags for the weekly discovery run; when unset it uses the line above.
#DEVLEAD_DISCOVER_CLAUDE_ARGS=--permission-mode acceptEdits --allowedTools Bash,Read,Glob,Grep

# The claude sessions always run through the image's own `claude` wrapper,
# which enforces the limits below: the container does not start with a
# DEVLEAD_CLAUDE_BIN that names anything else. Leave it unset.

# --- Schedule (S11, S16) -----------------------------------------------------------
# The jobs run inside the container on these schedules (supercronic). A run
# missed while the container or the machine was down is never made up.
# Time zone of the schedule and of the daily session count, as a zone name
# (America/Bogota, Europe/Madrid); empty means UTC.
TZ=
# One cron expression per job — five fields: minute hour day-of-month month
# day-of-week (0 or 7 is Sunday; names like mon-fri work) — or "off" to never
# run it. An empty value means the default shown. An invalid one stops the
# container from starting, and says which.
#   morning: the digest and today's agenda (sweep.sh; no claude session)
DEVLEAD_CRON_MORNING=30 6 * * 1-5
#   loop: the plan in ~/.devlead/plan.local.yml, when there is one
DEVLEAD_CRON_LOOP=0 22 * * *
#   fleet: one pass over every enrolled repo whose envelope is enabled
DEVLEAD_CRON_FLEET=30 22 * * *
#   discover: weekly exploration of the repos that enabled discovery
DEVLEAD_CRON_DISCOVER=0 5 * * 1
#   poll: new eligible issues (S4), checked with gh from bash; a claude session
#   starts only when there is new work, for those issues only and at most
#   budget.max_issues of them. New means never seen by the poll, whether the
#   plan includes it or cuts it for the budget. The first poll of a repo
#   records every eligible issue without starting anything (that backlog is
#   the fleet's). Default: every 30 minutes from 07:00 to 19:30.
DEVLEAD_CRON_POLL=*/30 7-19 * * *
#   endofday: the day's summary (S1) — runs, PRs opened, parked work units,
#   failed runs and the open PRs waiting for you — sent at level agenda. Plain
#   bash, no claude session; the journal stays yours (/cerremos).
DEVLEAD_CRON_ENDOFDAY=30 18 * * 1-5

# --- Limits (S17) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every claude session — scheduled or typed in the container — counts. One runs
# at a time; another one started meanwhile is refused, and a job that finds
# another job running waits for it. The count lives in a Docker volume of its
# own, so recreating the container does not reset it.
# Sessions per calendar day (in TZ). The next one is refused, and the job that
# wanted it sends a `need` notification.
DEVLEAD_MAX_SESSIONS_PER_DAY=8
# Time limit of one session, with its unit (s, m or h; at most 24h). Past it
# the session is stopped and a `need` is sent.
DEVLEAD_SESSION_TIMEOUT=60m
# Time limit of one whole job — syncing the repos, every gh call and every
# session in it — from DEVLEAD_SESSION_TIMEOUT up to 24h. Past it the job is
# stopped and a `need` is sent, so a hung step never blocks the jobs after
# it. Raise it for a plan that needs more sessions in one run.
DEVLEAD_JOB_TIMEOUT=4h
# How long a job waits for the job that is running (1s to 24h). Past it the
# job does not run, and a `need` is sent.
DEVLEAD_JOB_LOCK_WAIT=4h
# How many issues one run takes is budget.max_issues in each repo's envelope.
# Pause everything (no job and no session starts until you remove the file;
# only root can create or remove it):
#   docker compose exec -u root devlead touch /home/devlead/.devlead/PAUSE
#   docker compose exec -u root devlead rm /home/devlead/.devlead/PAUSE

# --- Audit (S18) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every job run appends one line to ~/.devlead/audit/YYYY-MM.jsonl inside the
# container (and to `docker compose logs`), and keeps the full transcript of
# each claude session in ~/.devlead/audit/runs/<run id>/ this many days.
DEVLEAD_AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# --- Egress firewall (S8) --------------------------------------------------------
# The container reaches only Anthropic, GitHub and the ntfy host. Add here, as
# host or host:port (default port 443) separated by commas, anything else the
# enrolled repos need, such as the package registries their tests install from:
#   DEVLEAD_EGRESS_ALLOW=registry.npmjs.org,pypi.org,files.pythonhosted.org
# Names are resolved when the container starts, and those are the only names
# the agent can resolve; restart the container after a change.
DEVLEAD_EGRESS_ALLOW=
